  "title": "Bands grow, single rings do not",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "For equally spaced networks of rule-60 rings with law (12,12) contacts: (1) every n x m torus of rings (n, m >= 3) has a half-turn fixing each contact and exchanging its rings, so every contact persists at every lag, and growth by inserting bands round the torus or by splitting every ring into k x l blocks keeps every contact persistent at every stage; (2) attaching one new ring to a balanced network breaks persistence: by one contact (a return of length 1), by two contacts not forming a bubble (one unpaired return of length 2), and as a bubble on the corner p -> q exactly when some old contact is reached from q and reaches p, since then D'_cc = 1 + w D_cq D_pc / (1 + w D_pq) (Sherman-Morrison).",
